## 4. Personas & Use Cases
1. **Nina (New Dev)** – Bootcamp grad building an admin dashboard. Needs sortable, paginated table today.
2. **Paul (Power Dev)** – Senior engineer at SaaS company. Wants to plug custom cell renderers, server‑side pagination, and theming that matches their in‑house design system.
3. **Maya (Product Manager)** – Cares about feature completeness (CSV export, column pinning) without negotiating licenses.

---

## 5. Core Principles
1. **“One‑liner to production, zero‑liner to customize.”** Sensible defaults; every surface override‑able.
2. **Performance first.** Virtualization baked‑in; minimal re‑renders; tree‑shakable modules.
3. **Design‑system agnostic.** Neutral base styles + optional theme packs (Material, Ant, Bootstrap).
4. **All features OSS.** No functional paywalls; optional sponsorship tiers only for priority support.
5. **Modern React.** Hooks, Context, Suspense‑friendly, SSR/React Server Components safe.

---

## 6. Feature Requirements

### 6.1 MVP (v 1.0)
| Category | Requirement |
| --- | --- |
| Data Display | Column definitions via `columns` prop; row data via `data` prop |
| Sorting & Filtering | Single & multi‑column; text, number, date operators |
| Pagination | Client‑side page & page‑size controls |
| Virtualization | Row & column virtualization auto‑enabled |
| Selection | Checkbox & click row select; exposes selection state hook |
| Column Resize/Reorder | Drag to resize; drag to reorder |
| Themes | **Butter‑Default** (neutral), **Butter‑Material** (CSS‑in‑JS), **Butter‑PlainCSS** |
| Accessibility | ARIA roles, keyboard nav (Tab, Arrow, Space, Enter), screen‑reader labels |
| Responsive Modes | Auto horizontal scroll; optional “stacked cards” on small screens |
| TypeScript | Fully typed generics; inference for `data` shape |
| Docs & Examples | Docs site with live CodeSandbox; recipes: basic, server data, custom cells |
| CI/CD | GitHub Actions: lint, type‑check, unit + perf tests, bundle‑size check |
| License | MIT |

### 6.2 Post‑MVP (v 1.1 → v 1.3)
* **Server‑side Mode** – Hooks for remote pagination, sort, filter
* **Tree & Group Rows** – Expand/collapse hierarchy, aggregation rows
* **Inline Cell Editing** – Built‑in editors (text, select, date)
* **Column Pinning & Visibility Toggle**
* **Export** – CSV & Excel export (web‑worker to avoid UI block)
* **Plugin API** – Register custom toolbar buttons, cell types
* **RTL & i18n**

